menu "PlantHub Wrappers"

config PLANTHUB_WRAPPER_ARENA
    int "Wrapper bytecode arena size (bytes)"
    default 4096 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32C5
    default 4096 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32C6
    default 2048
    help
        Size of the shared LRU-evicted arena holding LOADED wrapper
        bytecode blobs (M3 spec section 2), packed by their actual size
        rather than a fixed slot each -- this is what makes the 16-wrapper,
        2 KB-bytecode-each store affordable on a small part: the store
        itself is a flash limit (16 * 2 KB, LittleFS), the arena is the RAM
        cost, and the two are deliberately not the same number. A realistic
        wrapper compiles to a few hundred bytes, so this default holds
        several of them resident at once; only a pathological near-2 KB
        wrapper fills it alone.

        Both supported targets take 4096 (the C6 has 512 KB SRAM, the C5
        384 KB). The trailing 2048 is Kconfig's terminal default for an
        unlisted target, and is also the value tests/host/test_wrapper_arena.c
        exercises -- deliberately the tighter number, so packing and
        eviction are actually stressed by the host test rather than being
        given room to never evict.

endmenu
